counterfactuals.output:
An automatic fiber stripping system for removing a coating segment from an optical cable, the system comprising:

a cable holding unit configured to position and support an optical cable having a coating segment to be removed;

a pair of belt assemblies disposed on opposite sides of the optical cable, each belt assembly including a belt arranged to contact a corresponding side of the optical cable;

pressing portions configured to press the belts toward the optical cable such that the belts are tightened over the pressing portions and frictionally engage opposite sides of the coating segment;

a cutting unit including a blade movable relative to the optical cable and configured to form a notch at an edge portion of the coating segment; and

a drive unit configured to drive the belts after formation of the notch, whereby movement of the belts applies a peeling force to the coating segment from the notched edge and removes the coating segment from the optical cable.

In one embodiment, the belts are endless belts trained around rollers and are pressed inwardly by the pressing portions to clamp the coating segment therebetween. The blade may cut into the coating without substantially damaging an underlying optical fiber. After the notch is formed, the drive unit rotates the belts in a stripping direction so that friction between the belts and the coating segment peels the coating segment away from the optical fiber.
